cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use PyDebrisFlow2D in scientific work, please cite the exact
  software release used in your analysis. When an associated peer-reviewed
  publication is available, please cite both the software and the article.
title: >-
  PyDebrisFlow2D: A Conservative Python Multiphysics Solver for
  Variable-Density Debris Flows with Voellmy Resistance, Bed Exchange,
  and Grain-Size Segregation
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Secchi
    given-names: Mauricio
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-07-27
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  PyDebrisFlow2D is a modular finite-volume research solver for
  depth-averaged debris-flow propagation over digital elevation models. It
  includes hydrostatic reconstruction, HLL/HLLC fluxes, MUSCL reconstruction,
  SSPRK time integration, Voellmy-type basal resistance, variable-density
  mixture bookkeeping, bed exchange, grain-size segregation, and automatic
  CUDA-to-CPU fallback.
keywords:
  - debris flow
  - shallow-water equations
  - finite-volume method
  - Voellmy rheology
  - hydrostatic reconstruction
  - HLLC
  - MUSCL
  - CUDA
  - numerical modelling
  - geohazards
